                <pb facs="0922" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg824"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr.
                            Merry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Greytown</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-09-03"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 3,
                    1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm my telegram to
                    you of the 9th ultimo (13th?) and to inform you that I have now received the
                    written authorization from the Nicaraguan minister of foreign affairs to return
                    to the Bluefields merchants the duties deposited with me.</p>
                <p>I have therefore remitted the money to the respective depositors.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. P. Bingham</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">H. B. M. Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
